Dear Nanotechnology Professional,

Find your partner in Northern Europe! 

Nanotechnology in Northern Europe 2006
Congress and Exhibition
16-18 May 2006, Helsinki, Finland

NTNE 2006 is the largest nanotechnology forum in Northern Europe. This
unique event gives you the insight into latest research and industrial
developments and provides a great opportunity to expand your contact
network.

You have the opportunity to meet the key players from research to industry
with expected audience of 400-500 congress participants and up to 100
companies for the exhibition and surrounding events. 

Three main themes of the NTNE 2006 are:

Nanoelectronics and Nanophotonics
Molecular electronics, printed electronics, nanophotonics, optoelectronics,
quantum electronics

Nanotechnology Instruments and Tools
Instrumentation, metrology, modeling, software

Nanotechnology and Safety
Characterization, standardization and risk assessment 

Surrounding events include

 

IRC Partnering Event

Network of Innovation Relay Centres consists of 71 organizations including
all EU member states. This international partnering event allows companies
to market their technologies on-line in advance and prebook one-to-one
meetings with potential partners.

 

Finland's National Nanotechnology Programme

Finland has the largest national nanotechnology programme in Northern
Europe. 'Nanotechnology in Finland' symposium gives an up-to-date vision of
Finnish nanotechnology research and industrial perspectives.

 

IMAPS Advanced Technology Workshop (ATW)

IMAPS is a non-profit society for companies and institutions involved in
electronics packaging and production. ATW topics include opportunities
offered by nanotechnology for microelectronics packaging and challenges of
packaging of nanoelectronics.

 

CALL FOR PAPERS IS NOW OPEN!
Abstracts for contributed papers are invited primarily from the congress key
theme areas but other nanotechnology topics are also considered. High-level
contributions are selected by the scientific committee for oral
presentation. 

REGISTER NOW TO GET A GREAT EARLY-BIRD RATE!
Online registration is now open!

More information and registration:  www.nano.fi <http://www.nano.fi/>    

 

** If you do not wish to receive information on NTNE 2006, please send an
email titled 'unsubscribe' to info@nano.fi**

 


